    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog is headlined by **Lawrence Butler**, who commands the highest efficiency score of the day at 74.61. Despite being buried in the 8-hole, his massive 19% boost from facing a high-xERA arm in Littell, combined with favorable park factors and platoon advantages, makes him our anchor. We are also leaning heavily into the speed-weighted upside of **Dylan Beavers** (65.38) and **Masyn Winn** (59.10); both benefit from aggressive scouting of their respective opposing pitchers, Arrighetti and Pfaadt, whose slow deliveries provide a tactical edge for our stolen base-focused strategy. Meanwhile, **Bryce Harper** remains an automatic start at 63.62, bolstered by a strong xwOBA of 0.391 and wind blowing out, helping him overcome a neutral matchup against the southpaw Manaea.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Jung Hoo Lee**, who sat at a 47.73 efficiency score. He fell just short of displacing **Geraldo Perdomo** or **Taylor Ward** primarily due to the daunting task of facing Woo, whose 3.62 xERA suppresses base-hit potential too significantly for a contact-heavy profile. We are proceeding with **Yainer Diaz** (63.95) and **Gavin Sheets** (63.91) as high-floor pivots against Rogers and Dobnak, respectively, trusting their SP-skill boosts to outweigh the lack of premium lineup positioning. We continue to monitor the status of **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who remains sidelined on the IL, but with the current roster depth, we are well-positioned to maximize our daily caps while hunting for the scarce stolen bases provided by **Masyn Winn** and **Dylan Beavers**.",
